From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] WM Shell: let the user choose desktop-first on the internal
 display

DesktopDisplayModeController makes the default display desktop-first
(freeform windowing mode, apps open in desktop windows) while a
desktop-capable external display is connected, while an enabled
touchpad and an enabled full keyboard are present, or while the device
state reports a laptop hardware configuration. A tablet whose keyboard
cover stays connected over a wireless link after it is detached has
the touchpad and keyboard all the time, so its display would never be
touch-first, and an external display would turn the tablet's own
display into a desktop as well.

Add config_desktopFirstFollowsUserSetting. When it is set and the
internal display can host desktop sessions, the default display is
desktop-first exactly when the per-user Settings.Secure
"desktop_first_on_default_display" is non-zero, and touch-first when
it is 0 or unset. External displays, input devices and the device
state no longer change the default display; the input device listener
and the device state callback are not registered. The setting is
observed, and read again after a user switch. External displays still
become desktop-first on their own. The config defaults to false, which
keeps the existing behaviour.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific policy]
